Two licences, and why
---------------------

This is a fork of CivOne by Stefan Wouters (SWY1985), which was released as a
CC0 1.0 Universal public-domain dedication. The upstream dedication is kept in
this repository as LICENSE-CC0.md.

CC0 places a work in the public domain, so it may be incorporated into a work
distributed under any licence, including the GPL. That is what has happened
here: the combined work is GPL-3.0-or-later, while the upstream material it was
built from remains independently available under CC0 from the original project.

Relicensing the combined work does NOT withdraw anything from the public
domain. Anyone may still obtain the original CivOne under CC0 from upstream and
do as they please with it. What the GPL covers is this fork — the code written
after 2026-04-23 and the combined work as distributed here.

The same applies to material adopted from Christian Wimmer's parallel fork of
CivOne (https://github.com/ChrisWiGit/CivOne), which is likewise CC0 1.0.

    Upstream CivOne     CC0 1.0            last upstream commit 2019-10-14
    ChrisWiGit fork     CC0 1.0            adopted 2026-05 to 2026-07
    This fork           GPL-3.0-or-later   first fork commit    2026-04-23


Source file headers
-------------------

Most source files still carry the upstream CC0 header. Those headers are left
in place deliberately: for files inherited from upstream they are accurate
history, and rewriting 794 files would replace that history with a claim that
is true of the project but false of the file. The licence of the work as
distributed is the one stated here and in LICENSE.

New files may carry a GPL header. Neither header changes the licence of the
combined work.


Assets
------

No original MicroProse Civilization I data files are included in this
repository, and none are required to run the game. Where the game can read
original DOS assets it does so only if the user supplies them; otherwise it
falls back to art bundled here or generated at runtime. See PROVENANCE.md.


